}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395826 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eb2dd0d4-9bed-58b4-940b-d9ecf1e1866c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398053 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398053 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398053 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398053 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}$, find a basis for $\\text{Null}(A).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398053 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e63214c-016a-55f5-bcc6-73d6df35ee23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398053 #edb/ref 1074 "Any vector in $\\text{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}